  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Jsoup\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Jsoup\n       Program: jsoup\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Jsoup/Jsoup.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/jsoup.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Jsoup/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 93\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Jsoup-47\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\na025d87deb9cc4cda49ae1b77feb0f29805dd7c5\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2015-07-13 23:11:21 -0700\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\n528\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://github.com/jhy/jsoup/issues/528\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.jsoup.nodes.EntitiesTest::escapesGtInXmlAttributesButNotInHtml\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: expected:<<a title=\"[&lt;p>One&lt;]/p>\">One</a>> but was:<<a title=\"[<p>One<]/p>\">One</a>>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.jsoup.nodes.Entities\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Jsoup not retaining &lt in data attributes\nState: closed\n\nDescription:\nJsoup not retaining &lt in data attributes value if there is &lt;\n\nIn the example below &amp;lt; is converted to < in the output after parsing. \nPlease let me know how to retain it. \nExample:\nhttp://notes.io/Gww\n@uggedal \n@krystiangor \n@tc \n@bbeck\n\nComments:\n\n[krystiangorecki]: ~~Can anyone explain why do we parse html entities within `org.jsoup.parser.TokeniserState.AttributeValue_doubleQuoted`? Shouldn't all quoted values be left unchanged?~~\n\nWhen `data-params` attribute is parsed, it's internally stored as `{\"<p>Content</p>\"}` and it seems there's nothing wrong with it. This case probably invokes `toString()` which leads to `org.jsoup.nodes.Attribute.html(StringBuilder, OutputSettings)`:\n`86:             Entities.escape(accum, value, out, true, false, false);`\nand escapes `\"` back again to `&quot;` so the final result is: `{&quot;<p>Content</p>&quot;}`\nIt happens because when `\"` is found within attribute, it's escaped again to `&quot;`\n\n```\n                case '\"':\n                    if (inAttribute)\n                        accum.append(\"&quot;\");\n```\n\nbut `<` and `>` aren't\n\n```\n                case '<':\n                    if (!inAttribute)\n                        accum.append(\"&lt;\");\n                    else\n                        accum.append(c);\n```\n\nMaybe someone more experienced can explain this behaviour.\n\n@sandev \nIt seems to me that your original value is lost, but you can obtain unescaped value `{\"<p>Content</p>\"}` directly from Attribute:\n`doc.select(\"a\").first().attributes().asList().get(1).getValue().toString();`\nIt's ugly :(\n\n[sandev]: @krystiangor \n\nI think the correct fix should be something like below:\nI am testing it out to see if it is good in all scenarios. Please let me know your opinion.\n\ncase '<':\n                    // xhtml and in attribute\n                    if (inAttribute && escapeMode == EscapeMode.xhtml)\n                        accum.append(\"&lt;\");\n                    // NOT in attribute\n                    else if (!inAttribute)\n                        accum.append(\"&lt;\");\n                     // NON XHTML  and In attribute\n                    else\n                        accum.append(c);\n                    break;\n\n[krystiangorecki]: ```\nRunning org.jsoup.nodes.DocumentTest\nTests run: 11, Failures: 3, Errors: 0, Skipped: 1, Time elapsed: 0.107 sec <<< FAILURE!\ntestOutputEncoding(org.jsoup.nodes.DocumentTest)  Time elapsed: 0.004 sec  <<< FAILURE!\norg.junit.ComparisonFailure: expected:<...p title=\"\u03c0\">\u03c0 &amp; [&lt;] &gt; </p>> but was:<...p title=\"\u03c0\">\u03c0 &amp; [<] &gt; </p>>\n```\n\nbut after a small correction it seems to pass all the tests:\n\n```\ncase '<':\n    // xhtml and in attribute\n    if (inAttribute && escapeMode == EscapeMode.xhtml)\n        accum.append(\"<\");\n    // NOT in attribute\n    else if (!inAttribute)\n        accum.append(\"&lt;\");\n    // NON XHTML and In attribute\n    else\n        accum.append(c);\n    break;\n```\n\n[jhy]: It took me a while to understand this -- the allowed characters in an XML attribute are different to HTML\n\nHTML: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#attributes-2\nXML: http://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#NT-AttValue",
